{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed the problem by removing two throttling settings from the `rate` deployment, and the mitigation has been submitted. The submission returned 200. I haven't seen validation results yet.\n\n- **Root cause:** `rate` had `RATE_BACKEND_QPS_LIMIT=20` and `RATE_QUEUE_CAPACITY=256` set. They throttled the service, so `search` calls to `rate` failed with `DeadlineExceeded` and `ResourceExhausted`.\n- **Fix:** I ran `kubectl set env deploy/rate -n hotel-reservation RATE_BACKEND_QPS_LIMIT- RATE_QUEUE_CAPACITY-`. The `rate` pod restarted and registered in consul. I didn't check what default limits the service uses without these variables.\n- **Check after the fix:** `search` logged no new `rate` errors in the 20 seconds I looked after the rollout. The `Unavailable` errors in its log came from the pod restart."}}
